<title>JAPAN: Keihin Seiki shares jump on planned merger.</title>
<headline>Keihin Seiki shares jump on planned merger.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Keihin Seiki Manufacturing Co Ltd, a manufacturer of carburettors and other car parts, jumped on Thursday morning, supported by news on Wednesday that it would merge with two other car component makers from next April, traders said.</p>
<p>The share price was up 34 yen at 1,000 yen at 0103 GMT. Volume was 163,000 shares.</p>
<p>Keihin Seiki said on Wednesday that the two other companies, Honda Air and Device System and Denshi Giken Co Ltd, would be dissolved in the merger, which was aimed at boosting efficiency, competitiveness and investment.</p>
</text>
